{"id":"leetcode-3996","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Even Number of Knight Moves","summary":"Given two cell coordinates on an 8x8 chessboard, determine if a knight can reach the target in an even number of moves.","statement":"Given two cell coordinates on an 8x8 chessboard, determine if a knight can reach the target in an even number of moves. A knight move involves moving two squares in one direction and one square perpendicular to it.","constraints":["start and target are cells on an 8 by 8 chessboard.","A knight changes square color on every move.","Return whether the target is reachable in an even number of moves."],"topics":["graphs","chessboard parity"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"knight_even_move_reachable","parameters":[{"name":"start","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null},{"name":"target","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"bool","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def knight_even_move_reachable(start: list[int], target: list[int]) -> bool:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def knight_even_move_reachable(start,target):\n    return sum(start)%2==sum(target)%2\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def knight_even_move_reachable(start,target):\n    return sum(start)%2!=sum(target)%2\n","def knight_even_move_reachable(start,target):\n    return sum(start)%2==target[0]%2\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(1)","target_space_complexity":"O(1)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Color a cell by the parity of row plus column.","Every knight move flips that color.","An even number of flips ends on the starting color.","Compare the two coordinate-sum parities."],"editorial":"Compare the two coordinate-sum parities.","tes